<% content_for :title, "Ticket Delivery Policy" %>

<main class="policy">
  <div class="policy__wrap">
    <header class="policy__head">
      <p class="policy__kicker">Salato</p>
      <h1 class="policy__title">Ticket Delivery Policy</h1>
      <p class="policy__meta">Last updated <%= Date.current.strftime("%-d %B %Y") %></p>
    </header>

    <section class="policy__intro">
      <p>
        Salato sells digital tickets to events. There is nothing physical to ship —
        every ticket is delivered electronically the moment your payment is confirmed.
        This policy explains how you receive your ticket, what it contains, and what to
        do if it doesn't arrive.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="what-you-get">
      <h2>What your ticket is</h2>
      <p>
        Your ticket is a PDF document generated by Salato. Each ticket carries the
        attendee's name, a unique ticket number, and a single-use QR code. The QR code
        is scanned at the event to admit you, and it can only be used once. Keep your
        ticket private — anyone who has the QR code could use it to gain entry.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="how-delivered">
      <h2>How your ticket is delivered</h2>
      <p>
        As soon as your payment is confirmed, Salato delivers your ticket in two ways:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Email</strong> — the ticket PDF is sent to the email address you entered at checkout.</li>
        <li><strong>WhatsApp</strong> — the same ticket is also sent to the phone number you entered at checkout.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You only need one of them to get in — either the emailed PDF or the WhatsApp
        message will admit you, as long as the QR code scans. Delivery is usually
        immediate, but during busy periods it can take a few minutes.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="details-matter">
      <h2>Getting your details right</h2>
      <p>
        Your ticket goes to the exact email address and phone number you enter at
        checkout, so please double-check both before you pay. A mistyped address or
        number is the most common reason a ticket doesn't arrive. Enter the WhatsApp
        number in full international format (for example, +254 …) so the message can
        reach you.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="not-arrived">
      <h2>If your ticket hasn't arrived</h2>
      <p>If a few minutes have passed and you don't have your ticket, try this:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Check the spam or promotions folder in your email.</li>
        <li>Confirm the number you used has WhatsApp active on it.</li>
        <li>Make sure the email address and phone number you entered were correct.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Still nothing? Email <a href="mailto:hello@salato.app">hello@salato.app</a>
        from the address you bought with, or send your order number and the event name,
        and we'll re-send your ticket. As long as your payment went through, we can
        always re-issue it — the ticket is stored against your order.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="at-the-event">
      <h2>At the event</h2>
      <p>
        Bring your ticket on your phone or printed out. The organiser's team scans the
        QR code at entry. Because each code is single-use, once it has been scanned it
        can't be used again — so don't share your ticket or forward the QR code to
        anyone you're not giving your place to.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="responsibility">
      <h2>What Salato is responsible for</h2>
      <p>
        Salato is responsible for generating your ticket correctly and sending it to
        the email address and phone number you provided, and for re-issuing it if it
        fails to reach you through no fault of your own. Salato is not responsible for
        delivery failures caused by incorrect contact details, a full or blocked
        inbox, a number without WhatsApp, or your network or device. The event itself —
        entry, timing, and what happens on the day — is run by the organiser.
      </p>
    </section>

    <footer class="policy__foot">
      <p>
        Didn't get your ticket, or have a question? Email
        <a href="mailto:hello@salato.app">hello@salato.app</a>.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </div>
</main>

<style>
  .policy {
    --ink: #150D3A;
    --violet: #7620B1;
    --orange: #FC8027;
    --mist: #F7F4FB;
    background: var(--mist);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: "Inter Tight", "Trebuchet MS", system-ui, sans-serif;
    padding: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5rem) 1.25rem clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem);
  }
  .policy__wrap { max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto; }
  .policy__head { padding-bottom: 2rem; border-bottom: 2px solid rgba(21,13,58,.1); margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .policy__kicker {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: .8rem; letter-spacing: .04em; color: var(--violet);
    margin: 0 0 .75rem;
  }
  .policy__title {
    font-family: "Outfit", "Trebuchet MS", sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.05;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3.2rem);
    margin: 0 0 .9rem;
    background: linear-gradient(100deg, var(--violet), var(--orange));
    -webkit-background-clip: text; background-clip: text; color: transparent;
  }
  .policy__meta { margin: 0; color: rgba(21,13,58,.6); font-size: .95rem; }
  .policy__intro p, .policy__section p, .policy__foot p { line-height: 1.65; }
  .policy__intro p { font-size: 1.08rem; margin: 0 0 2.5rem; }
  .policy__section { margin-bottom: 2.75rem; }
  .policy__section h2 {
    font-family: "Outfit", "Trebuchet MS", sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 .8rem;
    padding-left: .85rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--orange);
  }
  .policy__section p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .policy__section ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; }
  .policy__section li { line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: .55rem; }
  .policy__section strong { font-weight: 600; }
  .policy a { color: var(--violet); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .policy a:hover { color: var(--orange); }
  .policy__foot {
    margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1.75rem;
    border-top: 2px solid rgba(21,13,58,.1);
    color: rgba(21,13,58,.7); font-size: .95rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .policy__section h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; }
  }
</style>
